# Example ReRDMFT input file: water, X2C spinors, MULLER JK-only
# functional, DEBUG TRUE. Besides the usual checks, the JK_only
# orbital-rotation validation report (main.cpp's
# jkOnlyRotationValidationReport) tests, for EVERY JK-only functional at
# generic fractional occupations and for complex spinors, the real-real
# (tt), imaginary-imaginary (yy) and real-imaginary (mixed) Hessian
# blocks, the joint real gradient vector [dE/dt; dE/dy] and the joint
# symmetric Hessian over [t; y] (Hessian_opt/JkOnlyHessian.h's
# jkOnlyJointHessianMatrix, the input of a Newton-Raphson orbital step)
# against finite differences of the gradient and, for MULLER/MULLER_AS,
# 2D finite differences of the energy (the true second derivative).
# HESSIAN_FUNCTIONAL TRUE additionally diagonalizes the full real-step and
# the joint (t,y) Hessians at the optimized occupations.
NELEC 10
BASIS water-sto-3g.gbs
X2C TRUE
FUNCTIONAL MULLER
DEBUG TRUE
HESSIAN_FUNCTIONAL TRUE

GEOMETRY
O   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.757000   0.586000
H   0.000000  -0.757000   0.586000
END
